      "text": "We begin by expressing each term in the sum as a fraction and rewriting the sum as\n\\[\\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{\\frac{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}}{x^{2^n}} - \\frac{x^{-2^n}}{x^{-2^n}}} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{\\left(x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}\\right) - 1} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{(x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}) - 1}.\\]We notice that this forms telescoping fractions, so\n\\[\\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{(x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}) - 1} = \\frac{\\frac{1}{x}}{x^{2^n}}\\left(\\frac{1 + x^{-2^n}}{1 - x^{-2^n}} + x^{-2^n} - 1\\right) \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{x}} = \\frac{1 + x^{-2^n}}{x^{2(n+1)}}(x^{-2^n} - 1).\\]Then\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \\frac{1}{x^0} + \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\left(\\frac{1 + x^{-2^n}}{x^{4n}}(x^{-2^n} - 1)\\right) \\\\\n&= 1 + \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\frac{1 + x^{-4n} + x^{-2(2n)} - 1}{x^{4n}} \\cdot \\frac{x^{-4n} - 1}{x^{2(2n)}} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\frac{x^{-4n} + x^{-4n} + x^{-4n} - x^{-2(2n)}}{x^{8n}} \\cdot \\frac{x^{-4n} - 1}{x^{4n}} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\frac{3x^{-4n} - x^{-2(2n)}}{1 - x^{-4n}} \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty (3 - \\frac{x^{2n - 2}}{1 - x^{-4n}}).\n\\end{align*}Note that for each $n \\ge 1,$\n\\[\\frac{x^{2n - 2}}{1 - x^{-4n}} = \\frac{x^{2n - 2}}{1 - x^{-4n}} \\cdot \\frac{1}{1 - 1/x^{4n}} = x^{-2n} \\sum_{m = 0}^\\infty x^{-4n m} = x^{-2n} \\frac{1}{1 - x^{-4n}}.\\]Then\n\\begin{align*}\n\\sum_{n = 0}^\\infty \\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= 1 + \\frac{1}{x^2} \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty (3 - 3x^{-2n}) \\\\\n&= 1 + \\frac{3}{x^2} - \\frac{3}{x^4} + \\frac{3}{x^8} - \\frac{3}{x^{16}} + \\dotsb \\\\\n&= \\frac{3.5}{x^2} + \\frac{3}{x^8} + \\frac{3}{x^{32}} + \\dotsb.\n\\end{align*}This sum is the coefficient of $x^{4k}$ in $\\frac{3(1 - x^{-2})}{1 - x^2} = \\frac{3x^{-2(2k)} + 3x^{-3(2k)} + \\dotsb}{1 - x^{-2}}.$  Therefore, the sum is $\\frac{3}{(x^2 - 1)(x^2 + 1)} = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{x^4 - 1}}.$. The answer is \\frac{3}{x^4-1}",
